{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אשר שנא ה' אלהיך", :translit "asher sanei hashem elohekha", :gloss "which YHWH your Elohim hates"} {:he "לא תזבח", :translit "lo tizbach", :gloss "you shall not sacrifice"} {:he "רובע ונרבע", :translit "rove'a venirva", :gloss "one who sodomizes and one who is sodomized"} {:he "מוקצה ונעבד", :translit "muktzeh vene'evad", :gloss "one set up [as an idol] and one worshipped"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut ha-parashiyot (juxtaposition of adjacent passages) links Deut 16:22 to 17:1"}], :frame {:text "Rabbinic hermeneutic principles of smikhut ha-parashiyot (juxtaposition of adjacent passages) derive that one who violates the prohibitions at the end of Deut 16:22 is rendered pasul (disqualified) for offering sacrifices, just as the immediately following verse (Deut 17:1) bars a blemished animal. Sanhedrin 108b lists one who sodomizes (rove'a) and one who is sodomized (nirva) among those barred from bringing a korban; the same page also addresses one who worships idols. Avodah Zarah 51b discusses that an object set up for idolatry (muktzeh) or worshipped (ne'evad) becomes prohibited for ordinary use.", :sources ["Deut 16:22" "Deut 17:1" "Sanhedrin 108b" "Avodah Zarah 51b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut ha-parashiyot (juxtaposition of adjacent passages) links Deut 16:22 to 17:1", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:37:02.491767366Z", :model "glm-5.2"}